OWED: `| some v` minting Src<live!> obliges the consumer arm — v must reach a `<!live>` consumer (dispose) or the flow refuses. MEASURED (2026-10): the transit rung landed — send consumes under `| ok`, the consumer arm mints `v: Src<live!>` via `__channel_obligate` — but auto-discharge silently settles the leaked `v` at the arm's leaf (it picks a compatible `<!live>` disposer — `__channel_take` or `dispose` — and inserts the call). The refusal this pin wants needs a compiler-level class: obligation minted at a transit boundary is NOT auto-dischargeable (`not_auto_dischargeable` in src/auto_discharge_inserter.zig exists per-binding but only for record-returns/unbound returns today; `~[strict]` is whole-file, too blunt for a generated unit). Blocked on a src/ semantic ruling, not the transform.
